Z||000000||FIERO1985||12-20-2000||08:10 PM||||anyone ever made a open header turn off before muffler so you can open and close and if so does it sound good or not"?<P>------------------<BR>1985 GT V6 <BR>"LETS RACE"||||reg||6
Z||000001||william_thorniii||12-20-2000||09:25 PM||||85,<P>Ummmmmmm no, not here at least.  I did experiece a sheared Y-pipe on my 85 GT once.  It was the gawd-awfulest sounding car you ever heard in my opinion.  I come from the old school of thought in that if your car is loud you had better mean business.  So I guess if I ever get a ZZ4 crate installed I would consider it... naaaah, a good burble at idle accentuated by a lumpy cam is all I want.  <P>I would suggest an investment in ear plugs if you decide to try this... oh and you can throw out your stereo too ;~)<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||1
Z||000002||2xsess||12-20-2000||11:19 PM||||I've had two EGR Vavles actually break apart on two different FIeros, the first being an 84 and the other on my 88GT. The both sounded awful with the exhaust not going through the whole system.<P>From what I've heard cut-offs almost always end up getting loose and sloopy causing leaks.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||fiero56||12-21-2000||12:00 AM||||And you lose some low end torque.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Standard||12-21-2000||01:12 PM||||Well, I almost have an open exhaust with my cracked-almost-in-half manifold... Not too loud at idle, actually.  And I think it sounds pretty cool when I tach it up at full throttle.. racecar, baby  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 153,000 miles and some busted up ground f/x  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/redface.gif"> <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/asthanos.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Xtreme Fiero's||12-21-2000||07:29 PM||||I ran my 84 SE (4-cyl) with only a Hooker Header & a DC sports Glasspack out the pass. side B4 the rear wheel. and with a modified timing & fuel curve it sounded like my buddys 99 LS1 Firebird with a real nice Borla system.||||reg||1
